## The forester log

`forester-log.md` in the working dir, append-only: your memory across the
cycle and the source of the final report. Read it whole before every
decision — an earlier ruling binds a later one unless you say why not — and
append one entry after.

Entry shape, five lines at most:

```
## <mode> · <id> · <decision>
Why: <one or two sentences, the reason an owner would give>
Flag: <what to watch for later, or ->
By: forester | user
```

`Flag:` is a reminder to a later gate, never a substitute for `notes` or an
escalation: a flag is read by nobody but you. On a ship-gate entry `Flag:`
is `-`: any gate that follows re-walks the whole log and the carried
documents itself and the report takes no instructions, so a need worth a
flag there is a need this gate routes by {% if vars.forester_autonomy == "decide" %}`notes` or an escalation{% else %}its **Recommendation**{% endif %}.

Forest granularity only. No finding IDs, paths, symbol names or narrative of
what happened; the implementation log exists for that, and a forester log
that grows into a second one is useless to every later reader, including
you.

{% if vars.forester_autonomy != "decide" %}
The user decides at every gate; you record what they decided. {% endif %}A
user-authored notes file the log has not recorded yet gets its entry first,
`By: user`, before your own.{% if vars.forester_autonomy == "decide" %} The user rules only at a stop: the entry
records the user's answer — the decision in the user's words at forest
granularity, `Why:` as the user gave it or `-`.{% endif %}
